# Living Survey: Artificial_General_Intelligence                                                               
                                                                                                               
## Introduction                                                                                                
                                                                                                               
This document collects the scientific literature regarding **Artificial_General_Intelligence**.                
                                                                                                               
## AGI Policy and Regulation                                                                                   
                                                                                                               
Recent discourse emphasizes the need for conceptual discipline and regulatory frameworks surrounding AGI       
development. The European Commission's call for AGI in healthcare has sparked debate on the risks and          
definitions of the term, highlighting the tension between advanced AI applications and the precautionary       
principle in EU policy[^10.1016_j.jrt.2026.100183]. Concurrently, strategic analyses track national            
initiatives, such as China's comprehensive roadmap aiming for leadership in general AI by 2030, underscoring   
the geopolitical race to achieve autonomous capabilities[^10.51593_20210064].                                  
                                                                                                               
## AGI Consciousness and Robotics                                                                              
                                                                                                               
The intersection of consciousness and general intelligence remains a pivotal area of inquiry. Theoretical      
frameworks propose that consciousness may emerge as a systemic capacity to integrate stochastic perturbations  
into stable gradients, positioning autonomous general intelligence as a mathematical inevitability within      
certain morphogenetic architectures[^10.5281_zenodo.19034234]. In parallel, investigations into robot          
consciousness explore whether sufficiently advanced general robotic intelligence could be indistinguishable    
from human consciousness, raising profound questions about substitution in responsible roles and the nature of 
artificial minds[^10.22339_jbh.v7i4.7403]. The broader question of whether AI systems can ever approach genuine
consciousness continues to drive intense speculation and research[^10.1109_mpuls.2024.3354609].                
                                                                                                               
## AGI Safety and Ethical Frameworks                                                                           
                                                                                                               
Ensuring the safety of AGI is frequently framed as a paramount objective, though critics argue that undefined  
systems like AGI resist standard safety testing. Some analyses suggest that the drive toward AGI is rooted in  
normative frameworks that may perpetuate discriminatory attitudes, using the language of safety to centralize  
power while evading accountability for harms to marginalized groups[^10.5210_fm.v29i4.13636]. Conversely, other
research advocates for a rigorous path to controllable AGI by building systems that provably satisfy           
human-specified requirements through advanced formal verification and mechanistic interpretability, arguing    
this is the only guaranteed route to safe deployment[^10.48550_arxiv.2309.01933].                              
                                                                                                               
## Philosophical and Strategic Perspectives on AGI                                                             
                                                                                                               
The pursuit of AGI intersects deeply with transhumanist and posthumanist philosophies, which envision          
technologies that strongly enhance human cognitive capacities. Debates continue regarding the promises and     
perils of super-intelligence, the commonalities between human and artificial intelligence, and how psychology  
can contribute to developing such systems[^10.1016_j.intell.2021.101563].                                      
                                                                                                               

